            "lens": "review-risk",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all 25 manifest paths for security, data loss and unsafe input handling; no reachable candidate-caused risk found.",
              "engine/skills/uninstall_plan.go: PlanUninstall refuses a procedural id or an id with no install record before planning, then reuses install's planSkill, so an edited, non-regular or unreadable recorded file refuses the whole uninstall and nothing is removed. The id from the command line only selects a lock record and is never used as a path.",
              "engine/skills/uninstall_plan.go: removeEmptyTree calls Remove only on directories holding nothing but empty directories. It deletes no file, so unrecorded files and their directory are preserved and reported as kept. A symlink entry is not treated as a directory, so it is not followed.",
              "engine/cmd/skills_install_cli.go: uninstall takes the exclusive project lock on the absolute working directory before any read or write, and refuses before locking when the working directory is not absolute. A dry run writes nothing.",
              "Confinement of recorded paths to the project is decided by the base install planner (planSkill), which this patch neither shows nor changes, so nothing is reported on it.",
              "The project-status change adds read-only output lines; the retryVerb change keeps the 'run install again' wording for install and adopt. The remaining files are docs, goldens, tests and review receipts with no runtime effect."
            ]
          }
        }
