            "lens": "review-resilience",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all 25 manifest paths for failure handling, retry safety, graceful degradation, observability, latency and load. No concrete candidate-caused production failure mode found.",
              "engine/skills/uninstall_plan.go: PlanUninstall reuses install's planSkill, so every refusal (edited, non-regular, or unreadable recorded file; no install record; procedural id) occurs before ExecuteInstallPlan runs and nothing is removed. Tests in engine/skills/uninstall_plan_test.go and engine/cmd/skills_uninstall_cli_test.go compare the tree before and after.",
              "Retry safety: a recorded file already gone is tolerated by the plan, and the install record is dropped only as part of the executed plan, so a rerun after a partial execution failure can finish. engine/skills/app/uninstall.go converts execution errors via executionFailure.",
              "RemoveEmptySkillDirs/removeEmptyTree are best effort, delete no files, and now report the cause of a directory that could not be removed (engine/cmd/skills_install_cli.go prints a distinct note); the earlier misleading-note concern is fixed and pinned by TestUninstallNamesTheCauseOfADirectoryItCouldNotRemove. Exit stays 0 with files and record gone, which is safe.",
              "Concurrency: engine/skills/lock.go makes uninstall take the exclusive project lock; the CLI takes it before reading and releases with defer. A relative working directory is refused before locking, with a test that no lock file appears. Overlay lock is not taken since no registry is read.",
              "Load: work is proportional to the files in one install record, with no network or registry reads. project-status change is read-only. Review receipts, README, usage, goldens and task notes have no runtime effect."
            ]
          }
        }
