            "evidence": [
              "All 25 manifest paths were reviewed for behavior, failure paths, determinism and test coverage. No candidate-caused reliability defect was found.",
              "engine/skills/uninstall_plan.go reuses install's planSkill with an empty source. An edited, non-regular or unreadable recorded file, an id with no install record, and a procedural id all refuse before any removal. engine/skills/uninstall_plan_test.go and engine/cmd/skills_uninstall_cli_test.go assert the tree is unchanged after each refusal.",
              "The dry run in engine/skills/app/uninstall.go writes nothing. The CLI test pins the 'plan: remove' and 'plan: update' lines and compares the whole tree before and after.",
              "Recorded files already gone, a missing runtime directory, unrecorded files (the directory is kept) and a directory that cannot be removed (reported with its cause) are each covered by a test in engine/skills/uninstall_plan_test.go or engine/cmd/skills_uninstall_cli_test.go.",
              "PlanUninstall sizes the new install list with len(c.lock.Installs)-1. This is safe because the record was found first, so the list has at least one entry.",
              "removeEmptyTree removes only directories and treats a symlink as a file entry, so it never follows one. The cleanup is best effort and cannot delete a file.",
              "engine/skills/lock.go makes uninstall take an exclusive project lock, and the CLI test checks that no overlay lock is taken. A relative working directory is refused before locking, and the test checks that no lock file appears.",
              "The project-status change in engine/skills/app/project.go lists the install records. The 'not in lock' error still fires only when neither a procedural skill nor an install record matches the id, and a CLI test covers listing, filtering, an unknown id and the state after uninstall.",
              "retryVerb in engine/skills/install_plan_skill.go keeps the 'run install again' wording for install and adopt, so their baseline messages are preserved. The golden files change only in the verb list, as the new verb requires."
            ]
